{%- comment -%}
  PG Line Fix: three cart repairs in ONE section, because slots are the
  scarce resource here.

  ================================================================
  WHY EVERYTHING IS IN THIS FILE

  A section group holds a MAXIMUM OF 25 SECTIONS. footer-group is at 24.
  themeFilesUpsert accepts a group JSON with more than 25 -- it validates on
  write -- but the storefront renders only the first 25 and silently drops the
  rest. That is the whole explanation for the last several rounds: files were
  written correctly, the API reported them correctly, and the page never
  contained them. It looked like a caching or propagation fault. It was a cap.

  So new work goes INSIDE an already-registered section rather than into a new
  one. Three fixes live here.

  ================================================================
  1. THE STRUCK PRICE IN THE STEPPER

  The line is a grid: "nm nm" / "vr vr" / "sv sv" / "qt pr" -- stepper in `qt`,
  price in `pr`. Separate cells, so nothing should collide.

  What collides is the CONTENT of `pr`. nc-linesave draws the price as a flex
  ROW with white-space:nowrap -- .nc-lsave-was (struck), .nc-lsave-now (price
  charged), .nc-lsave-off (pill). nowrap means it cannot break, and a grid
  item's default min-width:auto means it will not shrink below its content, so
  once was + now is wider than the column it overflows LEFT into `qt` and the
  struck figure lands on the + button.

  Stacked into a column, struck figure first. NOT a phone issue: the drawer is
  ~380-420px wide on desktop too, which is where it was reported. No media
  query. min-width:0 matters as much as the direction.

  ================================================================
  2. THE DRAWER MARK

  The disc used to be hidden in CSS in one file and replaced by JS in another.
  Two independent deliveries -- and when only the hide arrived, the cart had no
  mark at all, which is worse than the disc. So the hide happens in JS, on the
  line AFTER the wordmark is inserted. If this file fails to load or the drawer
  top is not found, the disc simply stays. There is no state with neither.

  Stamped inline because pe-logo, pg-drawer and nc-recs all write that element
  with !important and up to three ids.

  The mark is <a class="pg-wordmark"> so pg-wordmark kerns it -- that file
  splits the T into its own span, which is what stops it reading POCKE T ERA.
  Inheriting the class also inherits pg-mobile's HEADER sizing for it
  (clamp(40px,4.6vw,78px), scaleY(2.6), negative letter-spacing, all
  !important), so every one of those is re-set below on a doubled id.

  ================================================================
  3. THE UPSELL SENTENCE

  With one orb in the cart the row read "Add 2 more, get 1 FREE". True -- a Buy
  2 Get 1 Free pays out on the third unit, so the cart must reach three -- but
  it reads as though the offer moved further away the moment they bought one,
  and it leads with the demand instead of the offer. They pay for one more and
  two arrive. So: "Buy 1 more, get 1 FREE".

  The same edit is committed to pg-unlock, which owns the row and is where it
  belongs. It is rewritten here because pg-unlock is not one of the 25.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* ---- 1. the price cell keeps to itself ---- */
  html body #cart .l4ca > li section .nc-lsave,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li section .price,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li section .cols .price{
    min-width:0 !important;
    max-width:100% !important;
    display:flex !important;
    flex-direction:column !important;
    flex-wrap:nowrap !important;
    align-items:flex-end !important;
    justify-content:flex-end !important;
    gap:1px !important;
    text-align:right !important;
    overflow:visible !important;
  }
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-was,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .price .old-price,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .price s,
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .price del{
    order:-1 !important;
    display:block !important;
    margin:0 !important;
    font-size:12px !important;
    font-weight:600 !important;
    line-height:1.15 !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
  }
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-now{
    order:0 !important;line-height:1.2 !important;white-space:nowrap !important;
  }
  html body #cart .l4ca > li .nc-lsave .nc-lsave-off{
    order:1 !important;margin-top:2px !important;
  }
  html body #cart .l4ca > li section footer{min-width:0 !important;flex-wrap:wrap !important}

  /* ---- 2. the drawer mark ---- */
  #cart .pg-cart-mark{
    display:block;background:#0B0710;border-radius:12px;
    padding:13px 14px 10px;margin:0 0 8px;text-align:center;overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 8px 22px -18px rgba(0,0,0,.8);
  }
  html body #cart#cart a.pg-cart-word{
    display:inline-block !important;
    font-family:'Press Start 2P','Courier New',monospace !important;
    font-weight:400 !important;
    font-size:13px !important;
    line-height:1 !important;
    letter-spacing:0 !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
    max-width:100% !important;
    margin:0 !important;padding:0 !important;
    color:#F6DBFF !important;
    text-decoration:none !important;
    transform:scaleY(1.5) !important;
    transform-origin:center !important;
    text-shadow:0 0 5px rgba(246,219,255,.45),0 0 14px rgba(199,155,234,.32) !important;
  }
  @media(max-width:600px){
    #cart .pg-cart-mark{padding:11px 10px 9px}
    html body #cart#cart a.pg-cart-word{font-size:11px !important}
  }
</style>
<script>
/* PG Line Fix script RETIRED. The mark and the offer-row copy this ran every
   400ms are both owned by pg-unlock now; a second writer touching the same
   rows was one of the sources of the mobile drawer flicker. The CSS above
   still applies. */
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Line Fix", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
